  "answer": "500",
  "confidence": 0.99,
  "considered": [
    {
      "answer": "560",
      "reason_rejected": "Assuming the average of 60 applied to the whole week would give 7 × 60 = 420, then adding the extra 80 from the first three days (50+70+140‑420) leads to a different total; the problem explicitly says the average of 60 is for the rest of the week, not the entire week."
    },
    {
      "answer": "480",
      "reason_rejected": "Treating the ‘rest of the week’ as only three days (days 4‑6) would give 3 × 60 = 180, yielding 260 + 180 = 440, which contradicts the wording that a week has seven days."
    }
